      "writtenOn": "2016-10-12T23:43:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this true? AFAICT, getChip() and getChipId() do not return status codes. I\u0027m not sure if that\u0027s an issue with the commit message, or with the implementation.\n\n(Said differently: have you deliberately decided that getChip() and getChipId() should be available when the HAL is stopped? I understand that implementation-wise, it\u0027s possible to support that. But the question is more about the API: should callers expect these methods to be available, even before starting the HAL, or after stopping the HAL?)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "168a2ff9959aeb30e0aeb3945a99addd96cad8c1",
